-- title:
--   Faithful flatness detects ideals of R_𝔭
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings, let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime ideal of $R$, and write $R_{\mathfrak p}$ for `Localization.AtPrime 𝔭`. Let $\psi : R_{\mathfrak p} \to S$ be a ring homomorphism, and assume that $S$, regarded as an $R_{\mathfrak p}$-algebra via the algebra structure induced by $\psi$, is faithfully flat as an $R_{\mathfrak p}$-module. Let $I$ and $J$ be ideals of $R$ and suppose that their extensions along the composite $R \to R_{\mathfrak p} \xrightarrow{\psi} S$ agree, that is, the ideal of $S$ generated by the image of $I$ under $\psi \circ (\text{algebraMap } R\, R_{\mathfrak p})$ equals the one generated by the image of $J$. The conclusion is that the extensions already agree one stage earlier: $I\,R_{\mathfrak p} = J\,R_{\mathfrak p}$, i.e. the ideals of $R_{\mathfrak p}$ generated by the images of $I$ and of $J$ under the localisation map coincide. Nothing beyond commutativity and faithful flatness is assumed of $S$; the primality of $\mathfrak p$ enters only through the formation of the localisation.
--
--   This is the standard descent statement that a faithfully flat ring extension detects ideals, specialised to a localisation of $R$ at a prime as the base. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_algebraMap_localization_atPrime_eq_of_map_originChart_powerSeries_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_algebraMap_localization_atPrime_eq_of_map_originChart_powerSeries_eq), where $S$ is a formal power series ring receiving the local ring at the origin of a Weierstrass model, so that equality of two ideals read off in the formal chart yields their equality in the local ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_map_algebraMap_localization_atPrime_eq_of_map_comp_eq_of_faithfullyFlat.lean

